issue_context.body:
**Describe the bug**
After #26747 was merged I observed that some samples (hid-cdc, cdc_acm_composite) don't work anymore.
If USB stack is calling read transfer on every SUSPEND->RESUME it will quickly run out of transfer slots making it unable to finish the enumeration and make the device unusable.

Increasing the number of USB transfer slots does not help much. The issue could be seen when switching from virtual machine to native machine many times. Sooner or later there will be shortage of USB transfers and the device will no longer work.
``` diff 
diff --git a/subsys/usb/usb_transfer.c b/subsys/usb/usb_transfer.c
index 230337783b..9317b3bc8b 100644
--- a/subsys/usb/usb_transfer.c
+++ b/subsys/usb/usb_transfer.c
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
 
 LOG_MODULE_REGISTER(usb_transfer, CONFIG_USB_DEVICE_LOG_LEVEL);
 
-#define MAX_NUM_TRANSFERS           4 /** Max number of parallel transfers */
+#define MAX_NUM_TRANSFERS           20 /** Max number of parallel transfers */
 
 struct usb_transfer_sync_priv {
 	int tsize;
```

**Environment (please complete the following information):**
 - OS: Linux Mint
 - zephyr-sdk v0.11.2
 - 98bcc51b09 
 - Board: nrf52840dk_nrf52840. I haven't tested it with other boards but it also may happen.

**Additional context**
**EDIT**:
sample: cdc_acm_composite
board: nrf53840dk_nrf52840

Patch applied:
``` diff
diff --git a/subsys/usb/class/cdc_acm.c b/subsys/usb/class/cdc_acm.c
index 0f5f2ff50c..b0f8e2d0d6 100644
--- a/subsys/usb/class/cdc_acm.c
+++ b/subsys/usb/class/cdc_acm.c
@@ -416,6 +416,8 @@ static void cdc_acm_do_cb(struct cdc_acm_dev_data_t *dev_data,
 		LOG_DBG("Device connected");
 		break;
 	case USB_DC_CONFIGURED:
+		LOG_ERR("Configured, create transfer on ep 0x%02x",
+			cfg->endpoint[ACM_OUT_EP_IDX].ep_addr);
 		cdc_acm_read_cb(cfg->endpoint[ACM_OUT_EP_IDX].ep_addr, 0,
 				dev_data);
 		dev_data->tx_ready = true;
@@ -435,6 +437,8 @@ static void cdc_acm_do_cb(struct cdc_acm_dev_data_t *dev_data,
 		break;
 	case USB_DC_RESUME:
 		if (dev_data->usb_status == USB_DC_SUSPEND) {
+			LOG_ERR("Suspend->Resume, create transfer on ep 0x%02x",
+				cfg->endpoint[ACM_OUT_EP_IDX].ep_addr);
 			cdc_acm_read_cb(cfg->endpoint[ACM_OUT_EP_IDX].ep_addr,
 					0, dev_data);
 			dev_data->usb_status = USB_DC_CONFIGURED;
diff --git a/subsys/usb/usb_transfer.c b/subsys/usb/usb_transfer.c
index 230337783b..fa74db6ddb 100644
--- a/subsys/usb/usb_transfer.c
+++ b/subsys/usb/usb_transfer.c
@@ -127,7 +127,10 @@ static void usb_transfer_work(struct k_work *item)
 		}
 
 		/* we expect mote data, clear NAK */
-		usb_dc_ep_read_continue(ep);
+		ret = usb_dc_ep_read_continue(ep);
+		if (ret) {
+			LOG_ERR("Transfer error %d, ep 0x%02x", ret, ep);
+		}
 	}
 
 done:
@@ -203,6 +206,8 @@ int usb_transfer(uint8_t ep, uint8_t *data, size_t dlen, unsigned int flags,
 
 	key = irq_lock();
 
+	// usb_cancel_transfer(ep);
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(ut_data); i++) {
 		if (!k_sem_take(&ut_data[i].sem, K_NO_WAIT)) {
 			trans = &ut_data[i];
@@ -211,7 +216,12 @@ int usb_transfer(uint8_t ep, uint8_t *data, size_t dlen, unsigned int flags,
 	}
 
 	if (!trans) {
-		LOG_ERR("No transfer slot available");
+		LOG_ERR("No transfer slot available, print all transfers");
+
+		for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(ut_data); i++) {
+			LOG_ERR("Transfer on ep 0x%02x, status:%d",
+				ut_data[i].ep, ut_data[i].status);
+		}
 		ret = -ENOMEM;
 		goto done;
 	}
```
